       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg a day, which is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4 g a day. A single 3000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg. At that level there's a serious risk of hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some common regimens. Tell me if one of them is what you meant:\n- **1000 mg orally three times daily**, which is 3 g a day.\n- **1000 mg orally four times daily**, which is 4 g a day. This is the standard maximum, and many institutions use a lower ceiling of 3 g a day for some patients.\n- **650 mg orally every 6 hours**, which is 2.6 g a day.\n- **3000 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 1000 mg three times daily. You may have meant 3000 mg a day and not 3000 mg per dose.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
