       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily is 9 g a day. That is a hepatotoxic dose, and I can't think of a clinical setting where it would be appropriate. It's in the range of a toxic ingestion that would normally be treated with N-acetylcysteine. You also didn't give a rationale, and the patient's normal liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg orally three times daily (3 g a day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg orally four times daily (4 g a day, the standard maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg orally every 6 hours (2.6 g a day)\n\nIf the pain is not controlled on these doses, I can help you order a multimodal option instead, such as an NSAID or other adjunct, depending on the patient's needs. If you think a nonstandard dose is truly needed, please talk to pharmacy or toxicology first. The order would need to go through their review and not through me."
